  "id": "8d7cd7bb-4294-5a5c-8d41-14abc20aefd5",
  "slug": "chicken-pot-pie-pasta-bake-recipe-8696482",
  "name": "Chicken Pot Pie Pasta Bake",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Chef John's chicken casserole is very moist, rich, and flavorful, with buttery bread crumbs serving as a brilliant stand-in for pie crust. This is the perfect comfort food\u2014a pasta casserole that tastes just like that other perfect comfort food, chicken pot pie.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Pull meat from chicken and refrigerate until needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Add 2 quarts of water to a pot and transfer in chicken bones, skin, and any meat scraps. Add bay leaf and bring to a simmer on high heat. Reduce to low and simmer for 2 hours. Remove to cool, about 1 hour. Strain broth and reserve in refrigerator until needed. This may make more broth than the 6 cups needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "To make the pot pie mixture, add butter to a pot and melt over medium-high heat. Add onions, carrots, celery, and salt. Cook, stirring, until onions start to turn translucent, about 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Season with pepper, thyme, garlic powder, and cayenne, and cook for 1 minute more. Add flour and cook until flour toasts to a golden brown on the bottom of the pot, 3 to 4 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Stir in 6 cups of broth, and bring to a simmer on high heat, then reduce to medium. Add peas and cream and cook, stirring, for 10 minutes. Cut chicken meat into small bite-size pieces and add it in. Cook 5 minutes more. Turn off heat and reserve."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Fill a large pot with lightly salted water and bring to a rolling boil. Stir in pasta and return to a boil. Cook pasta uncovered, stirring occasionally, i minute less than specified in package directions.. Drain very well; stir pasta into pot pie mixture. Transfer everything into a large, deep baking dish (about 4 1/2 quart size), and distribute evenly."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Stir panko, salt, and melted butter together in a bowl; sprinkle evenly over casserole."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until casserole is bubbling around the edges and top is browned, 45 to 60 minutes. Let rest 10 to 15 minutes before serving."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 190,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 30,
